  },
  "repair": [
    "Immediately after each raw spawn, capture its backupAbortHandle and adopt into existing ConnectionPeer before any awaited/fallible setup step.",
    "Return guarded peers after successful setup. Dropping pending setup or its returned owner requests abort through existingDrop.",
    "Exchange and observer-send failures use existing finish_socks_route; alreadycompleted outcomes are observed and live siblings stopped with its existing5-second stop bound. Original two-second setup exchange/control observations remain.",
    "No completed error is converted to contextual text. The observer-closed context remains the original literal primary."
  ],
  "manual_layout_review": [
    "Grouped all preparation before spawn, each rawspawn+abortcapture+guardadoption together, and exchange after both guards.",
    "Kept response status/body/readiness and independent observation/backup/assertion groups separate.",
    "Concrete guarded fields own tasks; AbortHandles only support later finitebackup and do not imply joined ownership."
  ],
